WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:05.505
The decades-long
opioid epidemic

00:00:05.505 --> 00:00:08.174
in the US was once
dominated by drugs like

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:09.801
heroin and oxy.

00:00:09.801 --> 00:00:11.553
But with the rise of fentanyl,

00:00:11.553 --> 00:00:13.304
perhaps the most
dangerous phase

00:00:13.304 --> 00:00:15.015
is now upon us.

00:00:15.015 --> 00:00:16.099
In the first two years

00:00:16.099 --> 00:00:16.975
of the pandemic,

00:00:16.975 --> 00:00:18.184
more people were killed

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:20.520
by fentanyl than ever before.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:21.896
The Covid pandemic helped

00:00:21.896 --> 00:00:24.232
pave the way for
fentanyl's ascent,

00:00:24.232 --> 00:00:25.608
as isolation and boredom

00:00:25.608 --> 00:00:28.069
drove people to
substance abuse.

00:00:28.069 --> 00:00:30.655
There have been
more than 165,000

00:00:30.655 --> 00:00:33.033
opioid deaths since
the start of Covid.

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:34.492
Most of those deaths involved

00:00:34.492 --> 00:00:36.995
synthetic opioids like fentanyl.

00:00:36.995 --> 00:00:37.954
Fentanyl was first

00:00:37.954 --> 00:00:39.289
developed as a stronger

00:00:39.289 --> 00:00:40.707
kind of painkiller.

00:00:40.707 --> 00:00:41.458
It's cheap

00:00:41.458 --> 00:00:43.835
and the street version
is abundant.

00:00:43.835 --> 00:00:45.253
It's more than 100 times

00:00:45.253 --> 00:00:47.005
more powerful than morphine

00:00:47.005 --> 00:00:49.966
and 50 times more
powerful than heroin.

00:00:49.966 --> 00:00:52.093
Just two milligrams of fentanyl

00:00:52.093 --> 00:00:52.802
around the size

00:00:52.802 --> 00:00:54.804
of a few grains of salt

00:00:54.804 --> 00:00:56.765
can cause a fatal overdose.

00:00:56.765 --> 00:00:58.558
Fentanyl is now infiltrating

00:00:58.558 --> 00:01:00.060
other kinds of drugs,

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:01.978
including heroin and cocaine,

00:01:01.978 --> 00:01:02.937
as well as counterfeit

00:01:02.937 --> 00:01:04.481
prescription pills.

00:01:04.481 --> 00:01:07.525
That means people with an
opioid addiction are at risk,

00:01:07.525 --> 00:01:10.028
and so are users of cocaine,

00:01:10.028 --> 00:01:11.404
black-market Adderall,

00:01:11.404 --> 00:01:12.947
meth, marijuana,

00:01:12.947 --> 00:01:14.365
and other substances.

00:01:14.365 --> 00:01:16.076
The powerful drug is often

00:01:16.076 --> 00:01:17.452
used to strengthen or stretch

00:01:17.452 --> 00:01:19.829
stockpiles of other illicit drugs.

00:01:19.829 --> 00:01:21.790
The precursor chemicals
used to make

00:01:21.790 --> 00:01:24.417
fentanyl are also
globally available,

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:27.003
according to the Drug
Enforcement Administration.

00:01:27.003 --> 00:01:28.338
A lot of illicit fentanyl

00:01:28.338 --> 00:01:29.339
is made abroad

00:01:29.339 --> 00:01:32.175
and smuggled into
the US through Mexico.

00:01:32.175 --> 00:01:32.884
In Florida,

00:01:32.884 --> 00:01:34.594
Governor Ron DeSantis

00:01:34.594 --> 00:01:35.845
described the situation

00:01:35.845 --> 00:01:37.806
as a problem of law enforcement

00:01:37.806 --> 00:01:39.474
and border control.

00:01:39.474 --> 00:01:41.559
He has responded by increasing

00:01:41.559 --> 00:01:42.602
Florida's penalties

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:44.604
for opioid sale and distribution,

00:01:44.604 --> 00:01:46.022
and he announced a program

00:01:46.022 --> 00:01:47.315
that connects patients

00:01:47.315 --> 00:01:48.149
with treatments

00:01:48.149 --> 00:01:50.193
like naltrexone and methadone

00:01:50.193 --> 00:01:51.569
to help treat addiction.

00:01:51.569 --> 00:01:52.487
Similar techniques,

00:01:52.487 --> 00:01:53.863
like syringe exchanges

00:01:53.863 --> 00:01:55.573
are part of what's known as

00:01:55.573 --> 00:01:56.616
harm reduction,

00:01:56.616 --> 00:01:58.451
a movement
to decrease the risks

00:01:58.451 --> 00:02:00.370
associated with drug use.

00:02:00.370 --> 00:02:03.039
But some harm-reduction
techniques have been rejected

00:02:03.039 --> 00:02:04.958
by conservative elected officials

00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:07.544
who say they instead
enable drug use.

00:02:07.544 --> 00:02:09.587
Another tactic is the distribution

00:02:09.587 --> 00:02:10.755
of fentanyl strips,

00:02:10.755 --> 00:02:12.132
which can be used to test

00:02:12.132 --> 00:02:13.424
for the powerful substance

00:02:13.424 --> 00:02:14.467
in other drugs.

00:02:14.467 --> 00:02:15.844
But the strips are considered

00:02:15.844 --> 00:02:17.554
illegal drug paraphernalia

00:02:17.554 --> 00:02:19.597
in about half of US states,

00:02:19.597 --> 00:02:20.557
including Florida,

00:02:20.557 --> 00:02:22.267
according to Kaiser Health News.

00:02:22.267 --> 00:02:23.768
Florida's Republican-controlled

00:02:23.768 --> 00:02:26.271
legislature recently
shut down an effort

00:02:26.271 --> 00:02:27.147
to change that.

00:02:27.147 --> 00:02:27.897
In Florida,

00:02:27.897 --> 00:02:29.232
which skews older

00:02:29.232 --> 00:02:31.317
and is more than
a quarter Hispanic,

00:02:31.317 --> 00:02:32.694
most of those
who are dying

00:02:32.694 --> 00:02:34.320
of opioid overdoses are white,

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:36.990
and more than half
are younger than 45.

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:39.200
But with fentanyl use
on the upswing,

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:41.119
the death rate among
Black people

00:02:41.119 --> 00:02:42.996
has overtaken White people,

00:02:42.996 --> 00:02:44.122
and overdoses among

00:02:44.122 --> 00:02:45.665
Native Americans are also

00:02:45.665 --> 00:02:49.169
increasing disproportionately.

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:04.809
And we have a crisis

00:03:04.809 --> 00:03:06.311
at the US-Mexico border

00:03:06.311 --> 00:03:07.687
over the past year

00:03:07.687 --> 00:03:08.438
that's witnessed

00:03:08.438 --> 00:03:11.566
staggering amounts
of illegal migration

00:03:11.566 --> 00:03:13.067
and a massive influx of

00:03:13.067 --> 00:03:15.445
narcotics such as fentanyl.

